{"id": "EUVD-2026-59250", "enisaUuid": "478a8d3a-4cb7-394d-9477-399ed3785dab", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ngue: validate REMCSUM private option length\n\nGUE private flags can indicate that remote checksum offload metadata is\npresent. The private flags field itself is accounted for by\nguehdr_flags_len(), but guehdr_priv_flags_len() currently returns 0 even\nwhen GUE_PFLAG_REMCSUM is set.\n\nThis lets a packet with only the private flags field pass\nvalidate_gue_flags(), after which gue_remcsum() and gue_gro_remcsum()\nread the missing REMCSUM start/offset fields from the following bytes.\n\nAccount for GUE_PLEN_REMCSUM when GUE_PFLAG_REMCSUM is present so that\nmalformed packets are rejected during option validation.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:55:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:55:19", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/158b9995d3c87f3b93f5c22df54a12e12a3438b3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7c6876ec1b227261b51803f784c7be1b2242a1a0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2c4de9988e9ddc760b750d6b6e701c35ff60ad14", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2a99224c120823987e4d829726f4ecb33e03fc1e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/61e78679c7c9ca685bff58e4b6348304dc60aafd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4a4a1d41c6e901e773bcf795f562a47fa71f692a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f618cbe9b24cd0202004d2db781d5f80ab77037f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d335dcc6f521571d57117b8deeebc940836e5450"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-72351", "GHSA-pcv5-gx25-24wj"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.75, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "003498b8-5388-3d31-acf1-a0589c71efc1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.261"}, {"id": "015198bd-ad49-3a10-b9c9-8f37e781746a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c1aa8347e73e40924